course: dictionary
lesson: 1451
title: A cascade of meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «The river fell in a cascade over the rocks.» Water is falling down rocks, so a cascade must be a small waterfall.
explain: Cascade can also be a doing word. «Her hair cascaded down her back.» Cascaded means fell or poured down quickly in large amounts. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it an action? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Cascade can mean a chain of events too. «A trophic cascade is a change at the top of a food chain that ripples down.» One change causes the next, and the next, like dominoes falling over one after another.
fact: A cascade is a small waterfall, or a series of small waterfalls going down rocks.
fact: A cascade can also be a large amount of something falling or hanging down, like «a cascade of flowers».
fact: As a doing word, «to cascade» means to pour or fall down quickly in large amounts.
fact: A cascade can be a chain of events where one thing causes the next, and the next: «wolves eat elk, elk eat trees, and trees shade streams and feed beavers».
fact: Wolves returned to Yellowstone National Park in 1995 after about 70 years, and the trees grew back. That chain is called a trophic cascade.
exercise: «The river fell in a cascade over the rocks.» What is a cascade here? | A type of rock | A loud shout | *A small waterfall | A large boat
exercise: «Her hair cascaded down her back.» What does cascaded mean here? | *Fell or poured down quickly in large amounts | Was cut very short | Stayed perfectly still | Grew slowly on her head
exercise: «A trophic cascade is a change at the top of a food chain that ripples down.» What does this chain show? | Wolves always living alone | A sudden stop with no reason | *One change causes the next, and the next | A type of cake that is baked at the top
test: «The cascade of water thundered down the cliff.» What does cascade mean here? | A sad feeling in the chest | *A waterfall, or a large fall of water | A pet that jumps and runs | A shy look from a friend
test: What does «to cascade» mean? | *To pour or fall down quickly in large amounts | To lie still and sleep | To climb very high up a tree | To shine brightly in the sun
exam: In «Wolves returned to Yellowstone in 1995, and the chain it started is called a trophic cascade», what does cascade mean? | A big wave at the beach | A kind of tree that grows near rivers | *A chain of events where one thing causes the next, and the next | A chain of events where one thing causes the next
